**Choosing the reference and value**

* **Reference** – “U1” is the convention for the first microcontroller.
* **Value** – The value field is normally used to display the part number or
  a descriptive name.  We set it to “Arduino_Nano_Every” so the schematic
  immediately shows what the block is.

**Placement**

The KiCad coordinate system has the origin (0,0) at the lower‑left corner.
The A4 sheet is 210 mm × 297 mm, so a good centre point is
`X = 105 mm`, `Y = 148.5 mm`.  The module’s centre will be placed there.
No rotation or mirroring is required; the default orientation of the
